Human: In LaTeX, how do I make a set bracket with proportion symbols that use `\propto` when I want the two sides to have the same size, like `\left \{}...\right \}`?

Assistant: To create a set bracket in LaTeX that uses proportional symbols (`\propto`) with the same size on both sides, you can use the `pmatrix` environment from the `amsmath` package along with the `multirow` and `multlined` environments from the `mathtools` package. Here's how you can do it:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}
\usepackage{mathtools}

\begin{document}

\[
\left\=").\propto đội \left.)

\end{document}
```

In this example, the `pmatrix` environment is used to create the set bracket. The `multirow` and `multlined` environments are not necessary here because we are just adding two small proportional symbols. However, if you want to add more complex content or achieve different alignments, you can use these environments. The `pmatrix` environment is already in display mode, so the symbols `\propto` will adjust to the size of the bracket.

